Description: hw/input: Add the i.MX21 keypad port
 The Chumby's top button (the "squeeze switch", /dev/switch in the stock
 kernel) is on the i.MX21 keypad port, used as GPIO: the stock driver
 polls the data register and reads row 0, low while pressed. Its sense1
 driver uses the port for outputs too: column 2 powers the LCD and
 column 4 mutes the speaker amplifier.
 .
 Model the port's data register reading the pins configured as inputs
 (pulled up unless driven, through a GPIO input per pin), and a GPIO
 output per pin, numbered like the inputs, carrying the level on the
 pin: the output latch for pins configured as outputs, the level driven
 from outside (high when undriven) for inputs. Outputs are sent when a
 level changes. Scan interrupts are not modelled.
